course: dictionary
lesson: 6928
title: Padded: soft, quiet or extra
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The padded jacket kept her warm on the snowy walk.» A padded jacket has soft material inside, so padded means filled with soft stuffing to keep you comfortable.
explain: «The cat padded across the floor so quietly that nobody heard it.» Here padded is a verb, the past form of pad. The clue is quietly: the cat walked softly, not stuffed with anything. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Padded can also mean made longer with words that are not needed, as in «a padded essay». Read the whole sentence to decide, then swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense.
fact: Padded means filled or covered with soft material to make something comfortable or to protect it.
fact: «A padded envelope» is used to post fragile things safely.
fact: Helmets, knee pads and goalkeeper gloves are padded to protect you from bumps.
fact: «Pad» is a verb: «The cat padded across the floor» means it walked softly and quietly.
fact: Padded can also mean made longer with extra words or material that is not needed.
exercise: «The padded jacket kept her warm on the snowy walk.» What does padded mean here? | *Filled with soft material to keep warm | Walked softly across the snow | Very long and thin | Made of wet paper
exercise: «The cat padded across the floor.» What does padded mean here? | Made longer with extra words | Shouted loudly | Filled with stuffing | *Walked softly and quietly
exercise: Which of these is padded to protect you from bumps? | A tin of beans | A bicycle bell | *A goalkeeper's glove | A pencil case
test: «She sent the photo in a padded envelope so it would not bend.» What does padded envelope suggest? | *Protected, with soft material inside | Empty and flat | Painted bright red | Filled with water
test: Which phrase means an essay made longer with words that are not needed? | *a padded essay | a padded jacket | a padded knee pad | a padded envelope
exam: Which meaning of padded fits «He padded to the door in his socks»? | Filled with soft stuffing | *Walked softly and quietly | Shouted at the door | Made longer with extra words
